  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>In Six-Fours-les-Plages, Laverie La Baleine hosts a Dogwash station operated by Speed Laverie: a self-service dog washing system installed next to the regular washing machines, on avenue de Lattre de Tassigny. It works the same way as the other Dogwash network stations found across the Var: you wash and dry your dog yourself in about ten minutes.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Speed Laverie devotes a page to this Dog Wash: it is open 24/7, at 696 avenue Maréchal de Lattre de Tassigny, and costs €10 for the first 10 minutes, then €2 per additional 2-minute block — the same grid as the Hyères harbour dog wash, run by the same brand. The neighbouring launderette is open every day from 6:30am to 9:30pm. The type of shampoo supplied is not specified.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: since it's primarily a launderette, bring change or a suitable means of payment — the exact payment terms for the dog wash aren't detailed in the information available.</div>

      <h2>The programmes offered</h2>
      <p>The Speed Laverie page lists five programmes for the Dog Wash: hot-water shampoo, detangler, anti-parasite treatment, rinse and drying. Users build their own session from a touchscreen, with no appointment. Put your dog in the tub, choose the programme, then carry on: with 10 minutes for €10, it is best to have the order in mind before starting the clock. Remember to bring a towel; the site does not say one is provided.</p>
      <h2>A well-known spot in Six-Fours</h2>
      <p>Nice-Matin presented this station in September 2020, when the manager of the La Baleine self-service launderette installed it in the town centre, after seeing the concept (born in the Netherlands) at a trade show. The article then spoke of €10 for 12 minutes; the current Speed Laverie page announces €10 for 10 minutes. The business register (annuaire-entreprises.data.gouv.fr) lists a Speed Laverie Six-Fours Centre establishment at 696 avenue Maréchal de Lattre de Tassigny, open since January 2023: the station is indeed attached to this address.</p>
      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Six-Fours-les-Plages and its many beaches (Bonnegrâce, Le Brusc) are just a stone's throw away — handy for rinsing off your dog right after a swim.</p>
